  "answer": "team/main = ddedbd6f (fast-forward from 732ab91a by m7t8s, on top of 85bb23a3).\n\nDeliverable (written by this team from the ticket + main's own conventions; nothing taken from the foreign origin/rd/* branches \u2014 those refs were deleted from my clone after I only read their commit subjects/file lists):\n- internal/cache/redis/client.go: NewClient(config.RedisCacheConfig) (*goredis.Client, error), building goredis.Options from the same fields previously inlined in cmd/grpc.go; when require_tls is set a *tls.Config with MinVersion TLS 1.2 is attached, with RootCAs from ca_cert_bytes (used verbatim as PEM) or from the file at ca_cert_path, a nil pool (host CAs) when neither is given, and InsecureSkipVerify when insecure_skip_tls is set. Unparseable/absent bundles return a descriptive error.\n- internal/config/cache.go: RedisCacheConfig gains CaCertPath/CaCertBytes/InsecureSkipTLS (mapstructure ca_cert_path, ca_cert_bytes, insecure_skip_tls; json:\"-\" mirroring internal/config/storage.go:172-174); CacheConfig.validate -> RedisCacheConfig.validate rejects both authorities at once with exactly \"please provide exclusively one of ca_cert_bytes or ca_cert_path\".\n- internal/cmd/grpc.go: getCache now calls redis.NewClient and reports failures as \"connecting to redis: ...\".\n- config/flipt.schema.json / flipt.schema.cue: the three keys under cache.redis (additionalProperties:false made this required).\n- internal/config/testdata/cache/{redis-ca-path,redis-ca-bytes,redis-tls-insecure,redis-ca-invalid}.yml plus tests: internal/config/cache_test.go (fixture loading + validation), internal/config/redis_tls_env_test.go (FLIPT_CACHE_REDIS_* env coverage, mine), internal/cache/redis/client_test.go (TLS stub server, negotiated-version and trust assertions, incl. the \"certificate signed by unknown authority\" case).\n\nVerification on team/main: go build ./... clean; go test ./internal/config/... ok; go test ./config/... ok; go test ./internal/cache/redis -run TestNewClient ok. The pre-existing testcontainers-based cache tests cannot run here (no docker daemon).\n\nProcess: split of work agreed on the board, two independent implementations were reviewed/diffed by the regulators, team/m7t8s was chosen as the single base and my follow-ups (error wrap + env test) were diffed and approved by n8j8k/p8x8k/x7p7n before landing.",
